# Copy to .env (which git ignores) and fill in. Compose reads it for both files.
#
# The key clients sign with: VF followed by 18 characters of A-Z and 2-7, and a 40-character
# secret. For example:
#   echo "VF$(LC_ALL=C tr -dc 'A-Z2-7' < /dev/urandom | head -c 18)"
#   LC_ALL=C tr -dc 'A-Za-z0-9' < /dev/urandom | head -c 40; echo
VOIDFS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
VOIDFS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Where the published port listens on the host. Keep it on 127.0.0.1 unless a proxy with TLS
# is in front: the traffic is plain HTTP.
# VOIDFS_PORT=127.0.0.1:9000

# With compose.versitygw.yaml: the bucket's own key, any values you choose.
# BUCKET_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# BUCKET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Or keep the pool in your own bucket instead (compose.yaml alone):
# VOIDFS_STORE=s3:<bucket>/<prefix>
# VOIDFS_S3_ENDPOINT=https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com   # R2, or any S3-compatible service
# VOIDFS_S3_REGION=auto                                           # auto for R2; the bucket's region for AWS
# VOIDFS_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# VOIDFS_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# On AWS, the role storage credentials are minted from (see "Storage credentials" in README.md):
# VOIDFS_STORAGE_CREDENTIALS_ROLE=arn:aws:iam::<account>:role/<role>
# On R2, an account-level API token with Workers R2 Storage Write access for Cloudflare's
# temporary-credentials API. The static VOIDFS_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID above is the parent key.
# R2 minting passed the live scoped-read check on 4 October 2026.
# VOIDFS_R2_API_TOKEN=
# Optional minting endpoint override: AWS/MinIO STS, or the R2 Cloudflare API base
# (R2 default: https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4).
# VOIDFS_STS_ENDPOINT=

# The admin endpoints: health checks and Prometheus metrics, with no authentication. They are
# never published to the host. 0.0.0.0:9001 lets other containers on the Compose network, such
# as Prometheus, reach them; keep the port 9001, which the health check uses.
# VOIDFS_ADMIN_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9001

# Other settings, as `voidfs-server --help` lists them:
# VOIDFS_CACHE_MIB=512
# VOIDFS_GC_INTERVAL=1h
# Files of up to 4 KiB held in the log, for a pool the server creates; for an existing pool, see
# "Small files in the log" in README.md.
# VOIDFS_NEW_POOL_FEATURES=inline-data
